From 7d580199445835a1485e3e24d6686d44b12442fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: d0773d <dottedquad@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 09:08:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 41/48] video: fbdev: keep native one-shot scanout fed

ESP32-P4's DSI bridge emits its reserved pixel value when its FIFO
underflows. The reset value decodes as light cyan in RGB565, which can
hide a transient one-shot DMA starvation event behind an apparently
healthy framebuffer and clean masked underrun counters.

Program the reserved pixel value to black before enabling native DPI
output, and keep it as a checked runtime invariant. Match ESP-IDF's
minimal recurring DMA rearm transaction instead of repeating cold-arm
readbacks in every completion interrupt. Add passive transfer/rearm and
FIFO-depth telemetry so long disconnected runs can distinguish delayed
completion delivery from driver rearm latency without changing the
existing underrun policy.

Signed-off-by: d0773d <dottedquad@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/video/fbdev/esp32p4-dsi.c | 222 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 210 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/video/fbdev/esp32p4-dsi.c b/drivers/video/fbdev/esp32p4-dsi.c
index a8bff0a..460454f 100644
